
======================================================================================================
AUDIT: THE FROZEN DR4 PRE-REGISTRATION FEEDS nu THE OBSERVED, NOT THE NEWTONIAN, g_ext
======================================================================================================
  a0 = c H_Lambda / Z, Z = sqrt(32 pi/3) = 5.78881 -> a0 = 9.3600e-11 m/s^2 (canonical),
  = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_Lambda), exactly half the free-fall acceleration at the dark-energy
  density. kappa = 1/2 is this framework's own coefficient and is FITTED, not derived.
  Alternate footing 1.1300e-10 carried on every number below.

======================================================================================================
S1. WHICH ARGUMENT REPRODUCES THE FROZEN NUMBERS? -- the diagnosis, decided by arithmetic
======================================================================================================
  The amendments publish gamma^2_par = d(nu g)/dg|_g_ext and gamma^2_perp = nu(g_ext), then an
  orientation average. Two candidate arguments exist for a SINGLE observed external field:
     OBSERVED ratio   x_ext  = g_ext,obs / a0            (WRONG for nu, which takes y)
     NEWTONIAN value  y_extN = closure-inverse of x_ext  (what section 1.1 publishes)
  Feed each into the amendments' own formulae and see which returns the frozen table.

  primary g_ext,obs / a0_canonical = 1.899573

  Amendment 2 (alpha=1):  closure-inverted Newtonian argument y_extN = 1.464275
    argument fed to nu                   gamma_par  gamma_perp   gamma_avg   max|dev| vs frozen
    OBSERVED  x_ext                       1.011159    1.111526    1.079108             7.92e-04
    NEWTONIAN y_extN                      1.016888    1.138981    1.099791             2.75e-02
    frozen table                            1.0112      1.1115      1.0799
  [OK  ] Amendment 2 (alpha=1): the frozen numbers are reproduced by the OBSERVED ratio (max deviation 7.92e-04), NOT by the Newtonian argument -- so the amendment feeds nu the wrong argument. This is a computed diagnosis, not an assumption

  Amendment 3 (alpha=2):  closure-inverted Newtonian argument y_extN = 1.680884
    argument fed to nu                   gamma_par  gamma_perp   gamma_avg   max|dev| vs frozen
    OBSERVED  x_ext                       0.966904    1.052267    1.024603             3.27e-05
    NEWTONIAN y_extN                      0.963639    1.063063    1.030988             1.08e-02
    frozen table                            0.9669      1.0523      1.0246
  [OK  ] Amendment 3 (alpha=2): the frozen numbers are reproduced by the OBSERVED ratio (max deviation 3.27e-05), NOT by the Newtonian argument -- so the amendment feeds nu the wrong argument. This is a computed diagnosis, not an assumption
  [OK  ] Amendment 2: the two EIGENVALUES reproduce to 4.1e-05 (par) and 2.6e-05 (perp) on the observed argument -- tight enough that the identification is not a coincidence of rounding
  [OK  ] Amendment 3: the two EIGENVALUES reproduce to 3.7e-06 (par) and 3.3e-05 (perp) on the observed argument -- tight enough that the identification is not a coincidence of rounding

