    canonical cH_L/Z              1          1.464275      1.4647    4.25e-04
    canonical cH_L/Z              2          1.680884      1.4647    2.16e-01
    alternate rho_tot/cH0         1          1.150984      1.1513    3.16e-04
    alternate rho_tot/cH0         2          1.327952      1.1513    1.77e-01
  [OK  ] canonical cH_L/Z: the document's y_extN IS the alpha=1 closure inversion of g_ext,obs (deviation 4.3e-04) -- so the pre-registration DID compute the correct Newtonian argument, and the defect is that the amendments bypassed it
  [OK  ] canonical cH_L/Z: under the alpha=2 kernel now IN FORCE the inversion is 1.6809, which differs from the published y_extN by 2.16e-01 -- more than 20x the alpha=1 agreement. SECOND, INDEPENDENT DEFECT: section 1.1's y_extN is STALE with respect to Amendment 3's own kernel
  [OK  ] alternate rho_tot/cH0: the document's y_extN IS the alpha=1 closure inversion of g_ext,obs (deviation 3.2e-04) -- so the pre-registration DID compute the correct Newtonian argument, and the defect is that the amendments bypassed it
  [OK  ] alternate rho_tot/cH0: under the alpha=2 kernel now IN FORCE the inversion is 1.3280, which differs from the published y_extN by 1.77e-01 -- more than 20x the alpha=1 agreement. SECOND, INDEPENDENT DEFECT: section 1.1's y_extN is STALE with respect to Amendment 3's own kernel

