    canonical cH_L/Z         primary g_ext,obs     1.6809   0.96364   1.06306   1.03099        1.02460
    canonical cH_L/Z         alt Vc^2/R0           2.0242   0.96875   1.04726   1.02176        1.01816
    alternate rho_tot/cH0    primary g_ext,obs     1.3280   0.95924   1.08852   1.04720        1.03498
    alternate rho_tot/cH0    alt Vc^2/R0           1.6155   0.96269   1.06691   1.03334        1.02617
  [OK  ] CONCLUSION (i) SURVIVES: after correction all 4/4 alpha=2 combinations still sit below the frozen band edge 1.05 (corrected range 1.0218-1.0472). The argument error does NOT rescue the MI prediction into the frozen band
  [OK  ] CONCLUSION (ii) SURVIVES: gamma_par stays sub-Newtonian on all 4/4 combinations after correction (corrected range 0.95924-0.96875), so Amendment 3's pre-declared anisotropy SIGN is intact

  SIZE OF THE ERROR: the orientation-averaged gamma_v moves by 0.0036-0.0294 across all 8 combinations.
  For scale, the reproduction accuracy claimed for the frozen table is 4.1e-05, so
  the defect is 88x-716x larger than the
  agreement that was being cited as verification of that table.
  [OK  ] the smallest shift 3.61e-03 exceeds the 4.1e-05 reproduction tolerance by 88x, so this is a real defect and not numerical noise

  DIRECTION OF THE ERROR, measured as distance from Newton (gamma_v = 1):
     kernel footing                   |frozen-1|  |corrected-1|    which is more Newtonian
          1 canonical cH_L/Z             0.07911        0.09979                  AS-FROZEN
          1 alternate rho_tot/cH0        0.09364        0.12300                  AS-FROZEN
          2 canonical cH_L/Z             0.02460        0.03099                  AS-FROZEN
          2 alternate rho_tot/cH0        0.03498        0.04720                  AS-FROZEN
  [OK  ] the error runs CONSISTENTLY in one direction on the primary g_ext: the as-frozen numbers are MORE Newtonian than the corrected ones on every footing and both kernels. So the defect was making the framework's wide-binary prediction look CLOSER TO Newton than its own kernel implies -- i.e. it ran AGAINST a detectable anomaly, which is the direction that does NOT flatter the hypothesis

======================================================================================================
S4. NEGATIVE CONTROLS -- the diagnosis must be falsifiable
======================================================================================================
  A diagnosis that cannot fail is worthless. Two controls:

  [OK  ] control (a): a deliberately wrong argument x_ext/2 misses the frozen Amendment 2 table by 8.55e-02, so 'reproduces the table' is a discriminating test and not something any argument would pass
  [OK  ] control (b): the closure inversion round-trips y -> x -> y to better than 1e-25 relative over 5 decades for both kernels, so 'the Newtonian argument' is a well-defined object and the two candidate arguments are genuinely distinct quantities
  [OK  ] control (c) alpha=1: a = nu(y) g_bar reproduces a = a0 x identically (residual 0), confirming nu's argument is the NEWTONIAN y by construction -- the defect is a genuine type error, not a defensible alternative convention
  [OK  ] control (c) alpha=2: a = nu(y) g_bar reproduces a = a0 x identically (residual 0), confirming nu's argument is the NEWTONIAN y by construction -- the defect is a genuine type error, not a defensible alternative convention

======================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================
  TWO DEFECTS, both inside the frozen pre-registration, both confirmed by arithmetic:
   1. Amendments 2 and 3 evaluate nu and d(nu g)/dg at g_ext,obs/a0 = 1.8996 -- the OBSERVED
      ratio -- when nu takes the NEWTONIAN argument by construction (S4c). The document's own
      section 1.1 publishes the correct value, y_extN, and section 3's gate shape uses it;
      the amendments bypassed it. Same bug class as the forest chain in STANDING sec 5.1.
   2. Section 1.1's y_extN = 1.4647 / 1.1513 are the ALPHA=1 inversions. Under the alpha=2
      kernel in force since 2026-07-30 the inversions differ, so those published values are
      STALE with respect to Amendment 3's own kernel -- an independent defect.

  WHAT IT DOES *NOT* DO, computed rather than hoped: Amendment 3's conclusions BOTH SURVIVE.
  The MI prediction still sits below the frozen band edge 1.05 on every footing and g_ext
  convention, and gamma_par stays sub-Newtonian, so the pre-declared anisotropy sign holds.
  The correction moves the orientation-averaged gamma_v by a few times 1e-3 -- far above the
  4.1e-5 reproduction tolerance, so it is real, but far too small to flip a PASS/FAIL.

  WHAT THIS AUDIT DOES NOT COVER, stated so the amendment is not read as complete: only the
  framework-MI eigenvalues are recomputed here. Amendment 3's framework-as-MG row
  (1.0473-1.0885, a scalar mu(a_ex/a0) prescription) plausibly carries the SAME argument
  error, and the s^TX Door-4B numbers were not examined at all. Neither is corrected above,
  and neither may be assumed sound because the MI row has now been fixed.

  CONSEQUENCE FOR THE FROZEN RECORD. A frozen target may only be changed by an amendment
  filed IN THE OPEN. This audit does not change one. It establishes that Amendment 4 is
  OWED, and supplies the corrected numbers it should carry.
  NOT CLAIMED: any measurement of a0 (the pre-registration forbids that reading); any change
  to kappa = 1/2, which remains fitted; that the theory is closed.
======================================================================================================
